  "problem": "$(-2)\\cdot (-9)=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-2$ and $-9.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot (-9)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $2$ and $9$ without any signs: $2\\cdot 9=18.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot (-9)=18.\n$$",
